# Optional: T3 Connect for source builds
# C3 Code builds have T3 Connect turned off: nothing in them signs in to, or connects
# through, a hosted service. To turn it on against a relay and Clerk instance you run
# yourself, `cp .env.example .env` and fill in your own values. Do not add server-side
# secrets to this file.

# Your Clerk instance: from the Clerk Dashboard, under API keys, JWT templates, and
# OAuth applications.
# T3CODE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_...
# T3CODE_CLERK_JWT_TEMPLATE=...
# T3CODE_CLERK_CLI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=...

# Optional: signed macOS passkey builds. The RP domain defaults to the Frontend API
# hostname encoded in T3CODE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY. Set the override only when Clerk
# returns a different RP ID or when multiple domains must be entitled.
# T3CODE_APPLE_TEAM_ID=ABC1234567
# T3CODE_MACOS_PROVISIONING_PROFILE=/absolute/path/to/c3code.provisionprofile
# T3CODE_CLERK_PASSKEY_RP_DOMAINS=example.clerk.accounts.dev,clerk.example.com

# Your relay. `infra/relay` deploys update it automatically.
# T3CODE_RELAY_URL=https://relay.example.com

# Optional: hosted app origin used by the CLI's out-of-band OAuth flow.
# T3CODE_HOSTED_APP_URL=https://app.example.com

# Optional: your own Expo project, for EAS builds and over-the-air updates of the
# mobile app. Without it the app never checks Expo for an update.
# T3CODE_EAS_PROJECT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# T3CODE_EXPO_OWNER=your-expo-account
